# Copy to .env, run chmod 600 .env, then fill required secrets.
# Local setup placeholders only; deployment does not read this file.
# Fill every required value from your own configuration before local use.
# Compose has no fallback values.
# Only service environment settings are extracted. Ports, paths, networks and
# image versions remain in Compose, except the pre-existing image tag variables.
# See readme.md for first boot, storage preparation, registry login and migrations.
# Generate each password/token separately: openssl rand -hex 32
# Tempo passwords: at least 16 letters, digits, underscores or hyphens.
# Reuse actual passwords for existing databases; changing .env does not rotate them.
# Replace the public domains below and configure DNS/HTTPS proxy routes.
# Keep internal addresses/paths consistent with Compose and provisioning files.
# Media UID/GID must remain 0:0 for the documented rootless Docker setup.
# Transmission credentials below configure Digger's client, not the server.
# Configure matching Transmission server credentials separately.

COMPOSE_FILE=
USER_ID=
TIME_ZONE=
TEMPO_TAG=
GITEA_RUNNER_TAG=
DIGGER_TAG=
TRANSMISSION_USERNAME=
TRANSMISSION_PASSWORD=
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=
